Here's the standard pattern — put a `<video>` inside the div and position/scale it behind the content:

```html
<div class="video-bg">
  <video autoplay muted loop playsinline>
    <source src="video.mp4" type="video/mp4">
  </video>
  <div class="content">Your content here</div>
</div>
```

```css
.video-bg {
  position: relative;
  overflow: hidden;
}
.video-bg video {
  position: absolute;
  top: 50%;
  left: 50%;
  min-width: 100%;
  min-height: 100%;
  width: auto;
  height: auto;
  transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
  object-fit: cover;
  z-index: -1;
}
```

Key points:
- `muted` is required in most browsers for autoplay to work at all.
- `playsinline` prevents fullscreen takeover on iOS.
- The div needs some height (`height: 100vh` or whatever you want), and the content needs to sit above the video.

